# Design is not optional

The design spec for every Ghazal educational-panel and accounting UI change is **Emil Kowalski's skills**.

- Upstream: https://github.com/emilkowalski/skills
- Canonical copy in this repo: `panel-ops/skills/emilkowalski/`
- Index: `panel-ops/skills/emilkowalski/README-GHAZAL.md`
- Project skill: `.cursor/skills/ghazal-ui/SKILL.md`

Do not invent a second design system. Do not copy random dashboard CSS. Do not skip this because the task “is just a small CSS tweak”.

## First action on any UI work

Before writing or changing CSS, HTML, layout, a modal, sheet, button, sidebar, form, color, or animation, **Read** (do not skim from memory):

1. `panel-ops/skills/emilkowalski/skills/emil-design-eng/SKILL.md`
2. `panel-ops/skills/emilkowalski/skills/animate/SKILL.md`
3. Plus, when it applies:
   - sheets / press / spacing → `skills/apple-design/SKILL.md`
   - phone / tap / 100vh / 16px inputs → `skills/mobile-native/SKILL.md`
   - motion implementation → `skills/animate/RECIPES.md`
   - long names / empty states → `skills/break-ui/SKILL.md`

Those skills include an “I'm ready…” greeting. **Ignore that greeting** when this rule is already in effect. Follow the craft rules and write the UI.

## Never ship

| Never | Instead |
| --- | --- |
| `transition: all` | Named properties only, e.g. `transform` + `opacity` |
| `transform: scale(0)` enter | `scale(0.95)` + `opacity: 0` |
| `ease-in` on UI | `ease-out` / `cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1)` |
| Built-in weak `ease-out` on a deliberate motion | `--ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1)` |
| Drawer/sheet curve guessed | `--ease-drawer: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)` |
| UI duration > 300ms with no reason | 150–250ms (press 100–160ms) |
| Animation on something seen constantly (orbs, page chrome, 100+/day) | No animation |
| Ungated `:hover` motion | `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` |
| Missing `:active` on pressable | `transform: scale(0.97)` |
| Input font-size < 16px | `font-size: 16px` (stops iOS zoom) |
| `100vh` for app chrome | `100dvh` + `viewport-fit=cover` + safe-area env() |
| Tap gray flash | `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` |
| Laggy tap | `touch-action: manipulation` + press feedback on pointer-down |
| Animating width/height/margin/top | `transform` / `opacity` |
| Modal `transform-origin` at a trigger | Modals stay centered; popovers use the trigger |

`--ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(0.77, 0, 0.175, 1)` only for on-screen movement, not enter/exit.

## Review format

When checking UI you already wrote, use one markdown table with columns **Before | After | Why**. Not a bullet list.

## Product constraints (still apply)

- RTL Persian PHP panel. Map recipes to CSS; do not install a motion library for a fade.
- Do not restyle the English liquid-glass globally unless asked. Scope German to `.german-app` / `html.german-html`.
- Verify UI in the browser (or live CDP) before calling it done.
